WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:09.940
Gun laws have just been relaxed in the country
with one of the world's highest homicide rates.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.280
Brazil's far-right president Jair Bolsonaro
is reversing earlier, strict regulations that

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:23.470
essentially prevented civilians from bearing
firearms.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.730
In order to guarantee them (the citizens)
this legitimate right of defense, I, as president,

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:36.170
will use this weapon.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:42.090
The decree opens up gun ownership to adults
over 25 living in rural areas or high crime

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.870
urban areas.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:51.150
They must have no criminal record, and a gun
club course is obligatory.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:58.600
In a country that saw almost 64 thousand homicides
in 2017, Bolsonaro's hardline law and order

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.110
platform has won him support from those who
see wider gun ownership as a better way to

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:08.780
protect themselves.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.320
The new decree could increase violence but
at least it gives a chance to citizens to

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.600
defend themselves, if they are victims and
depend on police who aren't doing the job

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.570
they should.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:28.479
A recent poll by the Datafolha company though
suggests most Brazilians support the previous

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.710
restrictions on gun ownership.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:38.439
They fear more guns will mean more danger:
It's very clear in the decree that everybody

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:45.590
that lives in the country may have now the
right to own 4 guns.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:52.799
WEISSBLITZ It's an expansion of a license
to kill, that was seen before.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:56.170
I think that easing gun ownership is not good.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.639
I don't think that's the way we will improve
the situation in Brazil, it's not with fire

00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:04.299
against fire.

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:10.090
For now, Brazililan police and military are
still the only ones allowed to bear arms in

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.090
PUBLIC.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:17.080
The big fear for many critics is that it might
not be long before Bolsonaro allows civilian

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.190
gun owners to join them.

